<h2 id="gig-apps">Gig-app side hustles (fastest cash)</h2>
<p>If you need money this month, app-based work is the quickest path. The trick in Indy is to work the surges and skip the dead hours.</p>
<div class="hustle-grid">
  <div class="hustle-card">
    <h3 id="rideshare">1. Rideshare driving</h3>
    <p>Indianapolis is an event town, so rideshare is all about the calendar. Post-game rushes near Lucas Oil Stadium and Gainbridge Fieldhouse, Friday and Saturday nights in Broad Ripple, Mass Ave and Fountain Square, and early-morning airport runs are the money windows. Race weekends at the Speedway and convention weeks downtown can be the best-paying days of the year. See our <a href="/lyft-uber/">Lyft and Uber guide</a> for sign-up basics.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Pay:</b> $15–$25/hr before gas and wear</li><li><b>Startup:</b> Eligible car, insurance</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Night owls, event weekends</li></ul>
  </div>
  <div class="hustle-card">
    <h3 id="delivery">2. Food and grocery delivery</h3>
    <p>DoorDash, Uber Eats, Instacart and Walmart Spark all run busy in Indy. Suburbs like Carmel, Fishers and Westfield tend to tip better and have easier parking than downtown, while Castleton and the Keystone corridor pack restaurants close together. Dinner rush and rainy or icy evenings pay the most.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Pay:</b> $15–$22/hr before gas</li><li><b>Startup:</b> Car, bike or e-bike</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Flexible evenings</li></ul>
  </div>
  <div class="hustle-card">
    <h3 id="courier">3. Amazon Flex and package courier</h3>
    <p>With major Amazon facilities on the west and north sides and constant parcel volume, Flex blocks are common, especially around Prime Day and the November–December rush. Roadie and GoShare cover larger or same-day items. You see the block pay up front, which makes it easier to plan.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Pay:</b> $18–$25/hr (advertised block pay)</li><li><b>Startup:</b> Mid-size car or larger</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Early mornings, holiday season</li></ul>
  </div>
